menu "Michi SD"

config MICHI_SD_ENABLE
    bool "Enable microSD support (onboard card on the LCD SPI bus)"
    default y
    help
        Mounts the onboard microSD on the SPI bus shared with the LCD
        (CS 41, SPI2_HOST, same SCLK/MOSI/MISO as the display) and
        enables local OTA from the card (see michi_ota_start_local /
        michi_ota_check_local). The card is FAT, mounted at /sdcard.
        Without a card the system degrades gracefully: updates fall back
        to HTTPS OTA. The ESP32-S3 does NOT boot from SD - the card is
        update transport only.

config MICHI_SD_UPDATE_FILE
    string "Local update binary file name (on the SD card)"
    default "michi-update.bin"
    depends on MICHI_SD_ENABLE
    help
        Base file name of the firmware binary the receiver applies from
        the card. It must match the file:// base name inside the signed
        manifest (sign_manifest.py --url file://<this-name>), otherwise
        the update is rejected at validation. Keep it a plain name: no
        path separators, no ".." (the firmware enforces this).

config MICHI_SD_UPDATE_MANIFEST
    string "Local update manifest file name (on the SD card)"
    default "michi-update.json"
    depends on MICHI_SD_ENABLE
    help
        Base file name of the signed update manifest the receiver looks
        for on the card at /sdcard/<this-name>. The manifest is the SAME
        signed JSON used for HTTPS OTA (version/board/min_version/url/
        sha256/signature), signed with the same key; only the url scheme
        differs (file://<binary base name>).

config MICHI_SD_MOUNT_WAIT_MS
    int "Max wait for the async SD mount (ms)"
    default 3000
    range 100 10000
    help
        The SD mount runs in a task (michi_sd_init returns immediately).
        The boot-time local OTA check (michi_ota_check_local) waits up to
        this long for the mount flag before deciding there is no card.
        The mount usually completes in a few hundred ms while the rest
        of the boot runs in parallel (DAC/WiFi), so this is a safety
        bound, not a boot delay. Kept independent of MICHI_SD_ENABLE so
        michi_sd.c compiles unchanged when the SD support is compiled
        out of app_main/diagnostics (review F13).

config MICHI_SD_INFO_TTL_MS
    int "SD volume info cache TTL (ms)"
    default 30000
    range 1000 600000
    help
        michi_sd_get_info() performs the real esp_vfs_fat_info() SD I/O
        once and serves cached total/free bytes for this long. The
        diagnostics endpoint polls /diagnostics on demand; the TTL keeps
        the card quiet between polls. Kept independent of MICHI_SD_ENABLE
        so michi_sd.c compiles unchanged when the SD support is compiled
        out of app_main/diagnostics (review F13).

endmenu
